Author: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>
Date:   Sat Oct 10 12:22:20 2026 +1100

    common: Generate a timecost call id for every call
    
    timecost() generated its call id when it decorated a function, so every
    call logged the same id, and the start and end messages of overlapping
    calls such as concurrent get_routers() RPCs could not be paired.
    Generate the id per call, and keep the decorated function's name.
    
    oslo.utils' time_it() fixes its message when it is applied, so the
    wrapper now applies it on each call instead of once at import.
    
    Related-Bug: #1835663
    Prompt: while reading the L3 agent, Mikal noticed that timecost() mints
    its call id at import; a neutron-tempest-plugin-openvswitch log showed
    every get_routers() call sharing one id.
    Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context, low effort) <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context, low effort) <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
